 # W4 – The Toy Chest (place: look, cast, rule Bedtime, content)
 ## What exists
-- **Place** `toy_chest` (`data/crawloffame/crawl/places`, depths 1–9, weight 10, 3 green rooms, shop, 2 inhabitant rooms,
-  3 music rooms, 3 arrival lines); biome `toy_chest` (night-blue sky, violet fog, drifting dust), ambience
-  `ambient.toy_chest` (a slow music-box pad, clock tick), a music-box sting on a floor's first arrival; advancement
-  `crawl/toy_chest` ("Past Your Bedtime").
-- **Look** (`world.block.ToyBlocks`, art `tools/content/world/toychest.py`, `theme.ToyTheme`, `paint.Toy`, `ToyLooks`,
-  `ToyStages`): ~70 blocks drawn by script. **Three characters, each its faction's home**: the Playroom (walls of giant
-  wooden blocks with star/moon/ring/triangle reliefs in four colours, rug roads, crayons in four colours, star lamps:
-  the Regiment), Under the Bed (dark dusty boards, a slat lid low over the rooms with a strip of light at the edge,
-  lost things, glow stars: the things under the bed), the Dollhouse (wallpaper, wainscot, basket-weave parquet, cornices,
-  doll lamps, furniture a little too big: the Cuddlies). 12 combat looks (block tower, crossroads, toy town, the castle;
-  lost and found, the slipper, dust drifts, shoe box; tea party, the bedroom, the parlour, the music room); stages:
-  the General's top shelf (fort wall, cannon, towers), Old Buttons' bed (quilt, pillows), the Keeper's closet (double
-  door, the hand lamp's place), the zone's playroom floor (rug-road cross, two railway lines). Stairwells: the chest's
-  own dark mouth framed in crayons; corridors per character with waymarks. Great lamps over rooms (warm at play time,
-  blue at bed time). Generation 0.166 ms per chunk.
-- **Cast** (`mob.ToyMobs`, `ToyAbilities`, `tools/content/mob/toychest.py`, `toychest_anim.py`, 14 plans with painted
-  skins and clips, voices in `tools/content/audio/toy_sounds.py`): Regiment – Tin Soldier (rank armour, cork volleys on
-  order), Crank Box (tune, then springs down its marked line, stays open), Nutjaw (bites through a raised shield, orders
-  the volley), **The General of the Top Shelf** (fort, marble cannon; marbles roll back off the wall onto his side).
-  Cuddlies – Sock Puppet (gape, snap 4 blocks), Teddy Brute (opens its arms, holds and squeezes, two blows free),
-  Patchwork (falls into 3 pieces that resew it after 8 s unless all are finished), **Old Buttons** (charges; dizzy with
-  a thread out; pull it (use) and his seams open: armour off, ×1.5). Under the Bed – Lost Marble (rocks back, rolls
-  straight), Underreacher (drums, then grabs an ankle from under furniture), Night Light Eater (patch of dark: darkness,
-  bed things +33 % and ×0.67 damage taken), **Closet Keeper** (its own light/dark hours; in the closet untouchable, in
-  the dark ×0.25, in the hand lamp's beam ×1.25). Zone boss **Sir Gallopwood** (a rocking-horse knight galloping down
-  the rug roads after a 22-tick tell; the train knocks him off).
-- **Rule Bedtime** (`rules.floors.ToyRule`, texts `tools/content/rules/toychest.py`): the hours cycle (play 55 s, dusk 6,
-  bed 35, dawn 4) on the great lamps and the HUD. Play: toys +20 % speed, things from under the bed tucked away
-  (unseen, out of reach). Bed: toys sleep frozen (sneak past; a blow on a sleeper ×(1.5+bite), wakes it), the things
-  under the bed come out. Railway lines in most large rooms: throw the points lever and the engine runs the line,
-  striking monsters (and bumping crawlers); fort blocks (use) topple onto monsters; music boxes (objectives): winding
-  turns the hour and holds it 20 s; every box once opens the stairs. Softer at depths 1–2 (bite 0.6/0.8). HUD: hours
-  strip, boxes, held/bed lines; card line, hints, Emcee lines.
-- **Content**: uniques Rocking Lance (halberd), Winding Key (charm), Spare Button Eye (ring); Wendell Thimble (toy mender:
-  "Mending Day", quieten eight Cuddlies) and Posy Larkspur (night-light keeper: "A Quiet Night", a district boss);
-  8 achievements (Wake-Up Call, Points Taken, Wound Up and Ready, Loose Ends, Shelf Life Expired, Unstuffed, Nothing in
-  the Closet, Off His Rocker); searchable toy box, biscuit tin, piggy bank, locked jewellery box; voice script lines
-  (Emcee arrivals, rule, bosses; the network's hours; Wendell, Posy; recordings pending).
